# The hosts mikuterm connects to, in OpenSSH's ssh_config form.
# ~/.ssh/ is this folder's ssh/ (keys, known_hosts); a path without a folder
# is in ssh/ too.  Match, Include and ProxyJump are not supported.
#
# A host:
#
#Host server
#	HostName server.example.org
#	User me
#	IdentityFile ~/.ssh/id_ed25519
#	# Remote X programs as windows here (the host's sshd needs
#	# X11Forwarding yes and xauth):
#	ForwardX11 yes
#
# A remote desktop: the host's X programs drawn in one window of a size,
# the whole X screen (start a window manager or a desktop session there):
#
#Host desktop
#	HostName desktop.example.org
#	ForwardX11 yes
#	X11RootWindow 1920x1080
#
# The host's X programs' main windows as tabs of mikuterm's window, beside
# the tab of the connection (dialogs and menus stay windows of their own):
#
#Host tabs
#	HostName server.example.org
#	ForwardX11 yes
#	X11WindowTabify yes
#
# X11RootWindow and X11WindowTabify are mikuterm's own; for a file OpenSSH
# reads too, put "IgnoreUnknown X11RootWindow,X11WindowTabify" before the
# first Host line.
#
# WSL: [w] on a new tab's screen connects to a distribution's own sshd
# (port 22) without anything here.  A Host named wsl-<name> changes how one
# distribution is reached, for example when its sshd listens on another
# port (WSL's mirrored networking with Windows' own sshd on 22).  Without a
# HostName, mikuterm finds the distribution's address each time:
#
#Host wsl-Ubuntu-24.04
#	Port 2222
#	User me
